Title: Unsubscribe not called when using retryWhen
Description: I am not sure if this is expected, but when I run the below test, I get an assertion error:

`java.lang.AssertionError: Not unsubscribed. (1 completion)`

It does not happen all the time which is why I put it in a loop. I suspect it has something to do with the timer in `retryWhen`. If the timer is set to 0, the test runs successfully. Anything else, it fails. I noticed the timer runs on the computation scheduler and tried adding `observeOn(Schedulers.immediate())` everywhere with no luck. 

Is the expected? If so, how can I get this to run reliably?

Tested on RxJava v1.1.9 and v1.1.0

``` java

    @Test
    public void testUnsubscribe_shouldUnsubscribeAfterRetry() {
        String testValue = "test";
        for (int i = 0; i < 1000; ++i) {
            TestSubscriber<String> subscriber = new TestSubscriber<>();
            AtomicBoolean shouldFail = new AtomicBoolean(true);

            Observable.defer(() -> {
                if (shouldFail.getAndSet(false)) {
                    return Observable.error(new IOException("Network Error"));
                } else {
                    return Observable.just(testValue);
                }
            }).retryWhen(this::onErrorTryAgainWithTimer).subscribe(subscriber);

            subscriber.awaitTerminalEvent();
            subscriber.assertValue(testValue);
            subscriber.assertNoErrors();
            subscriber.assertUnsubscribed();  // Fails here
        }
    }

    private Observable<?> onErrorTryAgainWithTimer(Observable<? extends Throwable> errors) {
        return errors.zipWith(Observable.just(10, 1000, 2000), (n, i) -> i)
                .flatMap(time -> Observable.timer(time, MILLISECONDS));
    }
```


